WEBVTT

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.850
It'll pass by any minute now, Moka!

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.350
Yeah!

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.910
There it is!

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.080
Hey!

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.920
Isn't it amazing, Mike?!

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.430
Hey!

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.850
They waved!

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.730
Moka, let's definitely, definitely,

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:08.360
become Blue Mermaids!

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.020
Yeah!

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.320
Live on the sea!

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:11.900
Protect the sea!

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.780
Sail the sea!

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.030
That's...

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.530
...the Blue Mermaids!

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.500
Nine Years Later

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.670
And that's when...

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.220
C...

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:24.930
C...

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.140
Oh, a cat!

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.700
Ow...

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.870
- I'm sorry! Are you okay?!
- I'm fine.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:49.960
Sheesh.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.960
Watch where you're going.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.100
I'm so unlucky.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.190
Grab my hand!

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.900
No thanks!
I'm good at swimming fully-clothed.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.240
You're soaked.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.490
Drenched.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.700
And I've got the entrance ceremony to go to.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:25.950
You're unlucky, huh?

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.200
I don't want to hear it from you!

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:39.880
Yokosuka Girls' Marine High School
21st Entrance Ceremony

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.310
Your underwear
and uniform are dry!

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.020
I'll leave them here.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.150
I ironed them, too.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.650
Thank goodness you'll be
able to make it in time.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.900
Anyway, now we know
banana peels really are slippery.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.780
I'm going to change,
so would you leave?

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.040
Sorry, sorry!

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:15.040
Since we're both going to the same school,
I hope we can get along!

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:20.920
Mom? Do I look good in my uniform?

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.930
Moka!

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:32.890
Mike!

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.730
The ceremony is about to begin.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.190
I've already had quite a day.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.360
I thought you might not
make it in time.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:40.690
Sorry, sorry!

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.110
You never change, Mike.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.080
It's been a long time.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.210
Since elementary school, right?

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:56.420
Yeah.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.420
I guess they announce
the classes at the end.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.880
I hope we're assigned
to the same ship, Moka.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:07.180
<i>The entrance ceremony
will begin shortly.</i>

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.640
Yeah.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.350
<i>New students, line up.</i>

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.860
<i>Principal Munetani would
like to say a few words.</i>

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.990
Everyone, congratulations
on your admittance.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:25.240
I am the this school's prinicipal
Mayuki Munetani.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:29.780
You have all achieved excellent results
in classroom learning and practical skills,

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:33.160
and now you are students
of Yokosuka Girls' Marine High School.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.580
Your nautical training
will begin right away,

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.500
but I urge you
to overcome all difficulties

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.010
and become outstanding
Blue Mermaids.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.380
Wow, wow!

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:48.890
Moka, the Musashi!

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.760
Extra-large Direct Training Ship
Musashi
Captain
Moeka China
Deputy-Captain
Shouko Murano

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.760
And you're the captain!

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.890
That's great!

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.270
But Mike, you've become
a captain, too.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.600
Of the Harekaze.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.820
But the Harekaze is a destroyer-class ship.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.530
They don't even officially
call my position "captain."

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.360
Still, a captain is a captain.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.910
As a smaller ship,

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.990
you can get to know every inch of it,
so that's good, too.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.950
I see. When it comes to
actual number of crew members,

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.120
Musashi and Harekaze
have the same, huh?

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.670
Although it's automated
to a certain degree,

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.420
large ships are tough to handle.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.420
Though worth doing.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.300
I hope it'll be ok
with me as captain.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.800
I only studied the captain's job
while prepping for the exams!

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:33.890
I'm sure you'll make
a fine captain, Mike.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:37.390
Look. There's the Harekaze.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.940
It's kind of cute.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.320
So that's going to be my home.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:50.280
We're finally reunited,
only to be separated again.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:57.290
It's okay. We'll be on different ships,
but sailing on the same sea.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:06:59.420
Mike.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.790
We'll both make new friends,

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.920
me on the Harekaze
and you on the Musashi.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:10.140
You're right. Comrades at sea
are all family, right?

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.390
Let's do our best, graduate,
and become Blue Mermaids!

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.100
Right!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:15.180
Live on the sea!

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:16.600
Protect the sea!

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.060
Sail the sea!

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.480
That's the Blue Mermaids!

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.440
The Blue Mermaids' motto!

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.900
That brings back memories.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:28.530
We used to say that too
when we were kids.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:37.080
Nautical training starts
right after the entrance ceremony, huh?

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:41.460
We have to stow our luggage,
then report to our respective ships' classroom.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:44.790
The cat from before!

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:47.670
It seems kind of arrogant.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.260
Someone called it "Isoroku" earlier.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.390
Isoroku?

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.720
I guess the cat hangs out in this area.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.730
You have more of a captain's air
than me, Isoroku.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:03.400
Where's the Hiei docked again?

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.730
They said Pier Three.

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:06.980
We'd better get our luggage
and then go to class.

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:06.980
Huh? That's the farthest one from here!

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.240
Right!

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.370
Then I'll see you in two weeks,
after nautical training is over, right?

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.660
Yep. Two weeks will go by
before we know it.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.410
So I'll see you soon!

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.170
Welcome to the Harekaze
Good luck! New students!!

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:32.180
Organization & Orderliness

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:32.180
We're in the same class!

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.640
<i>Why the Harekaze?</i>

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:38.640
<i>I'm one of the leftovers.</i>

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.180
Ms. Munetani.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.190
Long time no see.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:44.850
Cheer up.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:48.940
It must be some mistake
that you didn't become captain.

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:51.440
Because your grades are top class.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.370
We're on the same ship!

00:08:57.660 --> 00:08:59.080
I'm unlucky.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.290
Maybe it's fate.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:01.410
It isn't fate!

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.170
I'm Misaki Akeno.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:06.710
Your names are?

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:10.420
- Ms. Munetani, do you know her?
- No! She's a complete stranger.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:13.800
Harekaze
Destroyer Captain
Akeno Misaki
Deputy-Captain
Mashiro Munetani

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.800
Ms. Munetani? Mashiro Munetani?

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.010
You're the deputy-captain, right?

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:16.800
And you are?

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.850
- I'm the assistant engineer...
- Hiromi Kuroki?

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:21.390
Yeah.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:22.310
Nice to meet you.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.520
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.600
<i>Misaki... Akeno...</i>

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:25.900
Let's all do our best.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.820
Harekaze

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.990
Harekaze class.
Is every crew member here?

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:43.870
Captain!

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:44.620
Yes!

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.420
<i>Captain?!</i>

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:47.790
Rise!

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.420
I'm Furushou, your instructor.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:59.220
From today, you're high school students,
and so, you'll embark on nautical training.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.430
I'm sure there will be tough times,

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:05.770
but there's a saying,
"A calm sea never made a skillful sailor."

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:09.770
When you help your comrades,
endure severe weather,

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.780
and ride out the rough waves,

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:15.030
all of you will have grown even more.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:20.740
When you've returned to land,
I can't wait to meet you as fine sailors.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.790
I look forward to it!

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.750
All right, all hands, prepare to set sail.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.630
Welcome to the Harekaze
Good luck! New students!!

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:36.510
Welcome to the Harekaze
Good luck! New students!!

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.590
Excuse me, Instructor Furushou!

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.510
What is it, Ms. Misaki?

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:40.680
Um, why was I chosen
as the captain?

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:47.690
I mean, my grades weren't so great
that I should be captain.

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:51.690
Then let me ask you,
what is your ideal captain?

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.480
Well...

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.780
Something like the father of the ship.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:02.700
And, comrades on a ship are family!

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:05.870
Then become that.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.210
Become a captain
who's worthy of the Harekaze.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:23.930
Huh? Isoroku?

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.180
A cat?

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.770
Cute!

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:29.940
Again?!

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:35.730
Did you... I mean, Captain,
did you bring it aboard?

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.110
I think it boarded on its own.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:40.570
We have to prepare to set sail!

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.280
What do we do about the cat?!

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:46.700
We can't take it off now and it'll kill any rats,
so I say we leave it be.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.960
Excuse me?!
We're going to sail with a cat?!

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.880
Then Isoroku can be the admiral!

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:55.460
And it outranks me?!

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:56.670
That's right!

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:02.050
I'm Captain Misaki Akeno.
I look forward to working with you.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.430
I'm Deputy-Captain Mashiro Munetani.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:09.390
I am the secretary, Kouko Nosa.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.350
I'm Torpedo Officer Mei Irizaki.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.230
I'm sorry! I'm late!

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:16.570
I'm so sorry!

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:23.530
I-I'm Chief Navigator Rin Shiretoko.

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.620
Wh-What's your name?

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:27.120
Ar... Ar...

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:32.830
Artillery Officer Shima Tateishi, right?

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:34.130
Yeah.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:37.710
All right! Then take your positions, everyone.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:39.800
Prepare to set sail!

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.720
Crew members at the bow,

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:44.720
prepare to leave the harbor!

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:46.100
Raise the anchor!

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:54.020
Both sides, take her out
nice and slow at 150 degrees.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:57.020
Harekaze, set sail!

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:00.490
Forward, slow and steady!

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:03.410
With steam turbine ships,
don't you use the valve to—

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:14.920
Chief Navigator, operations!

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:17.040
Chief Navigator, operations!

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:20.590
Both sides, standard speed ahead,
no problems.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:21.800
Compass bearing 150 degrees.

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:27.600
Understood. Chief Navigator, both sides,
standard speed ahead, no problems.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.310
Compass bearing 150 degrees.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:38.480
Moka!

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.860
Moka!

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:01.460
Nishinoshima New Island

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:07.010
April 7th 6:00

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:07.760
Have all the ships assembled?

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:10.010
No. The Musashi and Harekaze
aren't here yet.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:14.270
According to the message
the Harekaze sent, they'll be late.

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:16.770
What's our current position?

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:20.690
28 degrees, 10.5 minutes north.

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:24.860
139 degrees, 33.3 minutes east.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.280
72.4 miles to go.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:30.160
How many more minutes
until our destination?

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:33.950
A-At a speed of 18 knots,
four hours from now.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:38.250
Late to my first nautical training session.

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:39.830
I'm so unlucky.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:43.920
I-I'm sorry! It's because
I made a directional error earlier.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:46.550
And the engine came to a full stop.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.220
That's because the Harekaze
is a high-pressure ship.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:51.930
It's got speed, but also a lot of faults.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.100
I'm so unlucky.

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:57.270
By the way, where's the captain?

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:04.110
It's a beautiful day, right Isoroku?

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.280
The sea really is wonderful!

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:08.660
Captain!

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:11.030
The deputy-captain is calling for you!

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:12.530
Mei!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:16.200
She said that at this rate,
we won't make the rendezvous!

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:21.580
I had Communications Officer Tsugu
radio the Sarushima to say we'd be late.

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:23.840
She still told me to get you.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.210
Okay.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:31.590
What's wrong?

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.350
Where were you?!

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:34.680
Just on deck.

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:36.730
We're going to be late
and you're what?!

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:40.850
I had Tsugu radio them
to tell them we'd be late,

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:42.440
so I was feeding Isoroku.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:50.490
What the...?!

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.990
<i>Impact! Starboard 30 degrees, 3.0!</i>

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:54.410
Impact?!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.540
- The whole ship's shaking!
- What's going on?!

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:00.540
I'm 120% in the dark!

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:01.830
Another impact!

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.540
<i>A point-blank shot
has submerged the aft deck!</i>

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.840
<i>Cups are shattered in the galley!</i>

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:07.590
Shiro!

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:10.430
Shiro?

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:14.760
That's you, Ms. Munetani.
Your name's Mashiro, so "Shiro," get it?

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:15.810
Shiro?!

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:21.940
Captain. I'd like you to call me
either Ms. Munetani or deputy-captain.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.230
That's like being strangers.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:25.190
We are strangers!

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.780
Comrades at sea are family, right?

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:31.450
- We're not family!
- Anyway, Shiro, can I get on your shoulders?

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.580
Were you even listening to me?

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.830
Thanks! I can't reach it by myself.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:42.960
Captain! The Sarushima is bombarding us!

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:47.670
Instructor Furushou?!

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:48.760
Why?

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:50.260
Because we're late!

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:51.470
Of course she's mad at us!

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.300
Because of that, she's firing at—

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:56.680
<i>Impact on the port bow!</i>

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:59.890
It exploded? It's live ammunition?

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:02.770
At this rate,
we're going to have wounded people.

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:04.770
Rin! Take evasive action!

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.110
R-Roger!

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.110
That's right!

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:08.070
Shiro! Can you let me down?

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:08.860
Evasive action! Turn the rudder!

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:11.780
Coco, send a message
apologizing for our tardiness!

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:12.610
Roger!

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.030
Ms. Yagi! Radio the Sarushima.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:19.740
<i>Check, check.
We're really sorry for being late!</i>

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:19.740
The message is, "This is the Harekaze.
We're extremely sorry for being late!"

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:22.370
They're still firing!

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.000
They're just trying to scare us.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.420
If they wanted to sink us,
they would've already.

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.000
- Knowing the Sarushima.
- Captain!

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.510
They're not responding
to the message!

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:32.340
Are they that mad?!

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:33.130
Let me try!

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.760
I'll explain our reason
for being late.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:39.510
This is the Destroyer Harekaze.

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:43.980
We sincerely apologize for being
three hours and two minutes late.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:47.980
However, we had engine trouble,
so it could not be helped.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:51.110
This is a common occurance
among high-pressure ships.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:51.110
- It's like a textbook apology.
- Yeah.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:52.820
In other words, an unfor—

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.740
<i>Impact off the starboard side!</i>

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:58.200
They're striking closer
to home than before!

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:00.120
Let's just counterattack!

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:02.160
Ms. Noma! Signal them with flags!

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:02.830
<i>Roger!</i>

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:07.330
We-are-sor-ry!

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:08.920
Impact!

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:17.390
The engine room is flooding!

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:19.680
The quick reloader is broken!

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:22.310
The rice cooker isn't working!

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.390
Is anyone hurt?!

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:26.850
This is Maron Yanagiwara
in the engine room! We're all okay!

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:30.110
This is Himeji, torpedo tube two.
All right here!

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:31.780
Aside from the rice cooker,

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.360
Mikan Irako and two others
are fine in the galley.

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.240
<i>Impact!</i>

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.570
Their aim is becoming more accurate!

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:40.080
We've tried to change course,
but they still keep firing!

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.330
Are they attacking us seriously?

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:45.370
That cannon can fire 22 times a minute.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.670
Considering their radar sight,
their aiming is weak.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:51.000
Their rotating speed is slow, too.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.630
<i>Impact!</i>

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.600
Let's fire a torpedo.

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:04.470
A torpedo?!

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:07.640
Seriously?! We're going to fire?!
At them?!

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:11.520
In our position, all we can do
is try to withstand their bombardm—

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:14.980
Personally, I'd rather not attack.

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:17.780
But I have to protect everyone
on the Harekaze!

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:21.160
Because I'm the captain
of the Harekaze!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.370
If we fire a training shell,
they shouldn't sink, so it'll be ok.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:27.040
We'll try to stop their movement,
and escape during that time.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:27.790
Yeah.

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:29.000
Prepare for combat!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:30.420
Load the dummy shell!

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:32.250
Combat! Torpedo warfare!

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:35.380
<i>30 seconds to torpedo launch!</i>

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:37.630
Target sighted.

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:40.340
Bearing angle left 90 degrees,

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.760
target moving at 18 knots,
6,000 meters away.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:44.220
Get 3,000 meters closer.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.350
<i>In 20 seconds!</i>

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.150
In ten seconds!

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.400
<i>Ready to fire!</i>

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:54.820
Ready to fire!

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:56.280
Begin the attack!

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:12.830
Yes! Direct hit!

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:14.840
The Sarushima has slowed down!

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:17.920
Turn the rudder! Full speed!

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:19.300
Turn the rudder!

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.470
<i>Full speed!</i>

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:23.390
Go back! 0 degrees, steady as she goes!

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.850
Retreat to ten miles south of Torishima!

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:33.650
Jeez, it's hot in here!

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:35.940
Why did you all strip?!

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:37.280
It's so hot...

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:38.570
I'm dripping sweat.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:53.000
<i>Message from Yokosuka Girls' Marine High School's
instructor aboard the Sarushima.</i>

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.750
<i>They were attacked by student ship Harekaze
and took serious damage!</i>

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.340
<i>Students attacked them?!</i>

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:59.880
<i>Contact the Maritime Safety
Maintenace Bureau immediately!</i>

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.300
<i>This is the Haneda Port
Administration Bureau.</i>

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:03.930
<i>We've received a message
from the Sarushima.</i>

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:06.100
<i>They're asking for immediate action.</i>

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.770
<i>I repeat, this is the Haneda Port
Administration Bureau.</i>

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:10.680
<i>We've received a message
from the Sarushima.</i>

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:22.900
Still, why did they
have to bombard us?

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:26.780
Probably sudden special training
to see if we could really escape.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:29.040
That might be a possibility.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.870
But they were really
being serious about it.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.170
Maybe there was a coup d'etat
on the Sarushima!

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:40.510
This is no crummy
Blue Mermaids instructor ship!

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:44.840
I hereby declare this to be
the autonomous nation of Sarushima!

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.590
Why don't you think more seriously?!

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:49.260
But I'm glad no one
was badly hurt.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:52.390
It seems we all got off
with minor scratches.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.600
After we finish assessing the damage,

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.600
we should probably make a report
to the school, right?

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:59.110
I wonder how long they'll lecture us.

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:00.980
The radio. I'll get it.

00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:05.280
We'll just have to explain it to them
so they understand.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:07.870
Oh, no.

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:10.540
The Harekaze has...

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:13.250
Our ship has mutinied!

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:14.540
Mutinied?!

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:24.970
Episode 1: In a Pinch on Our Maiden Voyage!
